Subject: [PATCH] mcp: add Streamable HTTP transport

Targets Microck/kagi-cli v0.22.0 (src/cli.rs, src/main.rs, Cargo.toml).

Add a native HTTP transport to `kagi mcp` alongside the default stdio
transport, selectable with:

    kagi mcp --transport http --host <host> --port <port>

This serves the MCP Streamable HTTP transport: every POST body is handled as a
single JSON-RPC message (or a batch), requests return JSON, and notifications
return an empty 202 Accepted. The stdio path is unchanged in behavior; the
per-message handling logic is factored into mcp_handle_request so both
transports share it.

Adds the `axum` dependency (http1/json/tokio features only) and enables tokio's
`net` feature.

